note Exercism-style exercise "pascals-triangle": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/pascals-triangle
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note rows writes the first count rows of Pascal's triangle into o, row after row (1, 1 1, 1 2 1, ...),
note and returns how many numbers it wrote.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/pascals-triangle
om2
fn rows count ulong o edit ulong * to ulong
for r ulong count
s = div mul r add r 1 2
for c ulong add r 1
v = ulong 1
if and gt c 0 lt c r
b = sub sub add s c r 1
v = add get o b get o add b 1
end
put o add s c v
end
end
ret div mul count add count 1 2
end
